It seems that within the `onRestore()` of a bookmarked session, `callModule()` for nested modules isn't performing namespacing correctly. This causes nested modules to break.

Here's the simplest example I was able to come up with. There are two modules: outer and inner. The outer module contains a button that, when clicked, adds the inner (nested) module. The inner module simply contains some static text and a text output.

When you run the app and click the **add** button, the inner module will successfully get added. This is confirmed by seeing both the static and the output texts. I also print the inner module's output ID to the console, to see what it is, and it is correct (`outer-mod-test`). When you click the bookmark button and then try to restore the session, I use `onRestore()` to call the exact same code as the button called, but this time the output text doesn't show up, and the reason for that is that the output ID didn't get namespaced (you can see that by looking at the console output once again - it isn't namespaced `mod-test`). This might seem like a very contrived example, but I'm getting this problem in a real app.

```
library(shiny)

innerUI <- function(id) {
  ns <- NS(id)
  tagList(
    "UI content",
    textOutput(ns("test"))
  )
}
inner <- function(input, output, session) {
  cat("output ID:", session$ns("test"),"\n")
  output$test <- renderText("output content")
}

outerUI <- function(id) {
  ns <- NS(id)
  actionButton(ns("add"), "add")
}

outer <- function(input, output, session) {
  setBookmarkExclude("add")
  
  add_ui <- function() {
    insertUI(
      selector =  "body",
      where = "beforeEnd",
      innerUI(session$ns("mod"))
    )

    callModule(inner, "mod")
  }
  
  observeEvent(input$add, add_ui())
  
  onRestore(function(state) {
    add_ui()
  })
}

ui <- function(req) {
  fluidPage(
    bookmarkButton(), br(),
    outerUI("outer")
  )
}

server <- function(input, output, session) {
  callModule(outer, "outer")
}

shinyApp(ui, server, enableBookmarking = "server")
```

