This test app shows various ways `renderPlot()` and assigning to outputs can leak memory. (This is originally from https://community.rstudio.com/t/memory-leak-when-using-ggplot2-grobs-and-tabs-shiny-or-my-bug/30108/.) **Update:** I've also added examples with `renderText()`.

In the first case, `renderPlot()` is called in an observer and assigned to an output each time. It leaks about 76528 bytes each time.

In the second case, a `renderPlot()` is invalidated. This leaks 2352 bytes each time.

In the third case, `renderPlot()` is called in an observer, but it is simply discarded. This leaks 1480 bytes each time.

The next three cases are the same, but use `renderText()`. They leak 2352, 1168, and 1168 bytes, respectively.

```R
library(shiny)
library(pryr)

ui <- fluidPage(
  sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
      div(
