When using `renderCachedPlot` with async plotting code, the result is the error "Error in !: invalid argument type". Specifically, this happens when async plotting code is paired with a non-async `cacheKeyExpr`:

```r
library(shiny)
library(promises)
library(future)
plan(multiprocess)

ui <- fluidPage(
  numericInput("n", "n", 10),
  plotOutput("plot")
)

server <- function(input, output, session) {
  output$plot <- renderCachedPlot({
    n <- input$n
    future({ head(cars, n) }) %...>% {
      plot(.)
    }
  }, cacheKeyExpr = { input$n })
}

shinyApp(ui, server)
```

In this example, the main body of `renderCachedPlot` returns a promise, while `cacheKeyExpr` does not.

### Workaround

For now, you can easily work around this issue by wrapping the `cacheKeyExpr` argument in `promise_resolve`:

```r
library(shiny)
library(promises)
library(future)
plan(multiprocess)

ui <- fluidPage(
  numericInput("n", "n", 10),
  plotOutput("plot")
)

server <- function(input, output, session) {
  output$plot <- renderCachedPlot({
    n <- input$n
    future({ head(cars, n) }) %...>% {
      plot(.)
    }
  }, cacheKeyExpr = { promise_resolve(input$n) })
}

shinyApp(ui, server)
```

The `promise_resolve` function will take any value, and if it's not a promise, will wrap it so it becomes a (resolved) promise.

