I noticed that hovering or selecting points in plots from `renderPlot({})` gives shifted values for the values when par(oma) is not set to default values; I modified the example from  [here](https://shiny.rstudio.com/articles/plot-interaction.html) for clarification. Note that changing the oma values will change the directionality of the shift; with `oma(0,3,0,3)` as shown here, low x-axis values will be reported as a higher value and higher values will be reported as lower than they are. It also depends on the range - the shift can be quite significant (I have seen values up to 20% off depending on dataset).
So I don't use the oma() anymore but thought this would be interesting to people facing the same issue.


 
```
ui <- basicPage(
  plotOutput("plot1",
             click = "plot_click",
             dblclick = "plot_dblclick",
             hover = "plot_hover",
             brush = "plot_brush"
  ),
  verbatimTextOutput("info")
)

server <- function(input, output) {
  output$plot1 <- renderPlot({
    par(oma = c(0,3,0,3))
    plot(mtcars$wt*100, mtcars$mpg)
  })
  
  output$info <- renderText({
    xy_str <- function(e) {
      if(is.null(e)) return("NULL\n")
      paste0("x=", round(e$x, 1), " y=", round(e$y, 1), "\n")
    }
    xy_range_str <- function(e) {
      if(is.null(e)) return("NULL\n")
      paste0("xmin=", round(e$xmin, 1), " xmax=", round(e$xmax, 1), 
             " ymin=", round(e$ymin, 1), " ymax=", round(e$ymax, 1))
    }
    
    paste0(
      "click: ", xy_str(input$plot_click),
      "dblclick: ", xy_str(input$plot_dblclick),
      "hover: ", xy_str(input$plot_hover),
      "brush: ", xy_range_str(input$plot_brush)
    )
  })
}

shinyApp(ui, server)
```

