The most common use case is probably to be able to set `suspendWhenHidden = FALSE` for all outputs of a module, from within the parent app.

I think this is important enough to warrant its own issue, but it's not urgent, so I'm just registering it so we don't forget about it.

----

Here's what we have to today (no ability to set module output options from within the parent app that calls it):

```r
library(shiny)

modUI <- function(id) {
  ns <- NS(id)
  plotOutput(ns("p1"))
}
mod <- function(input, output, session, numPoints) {
  output$p1 <- renderPlot({
    Sys.sleep(1)
    plot(runif(numPoints()))
  })
}

ui <- fixedPage(
  tabsetPanel(
    tabPanel("Module", modUI("modID")),
    tabPanel("Other stuff", numericInput("points", "How many point to plot", 10))
  )
)

server <- function(input, output, session) {
  callModule(mod, "modID", reactive(input$points))
}

shinyApp(ui, server)
```

Here's what would be nice to have (mock up only; absolutely not working right now in any way):

```r
library(shiny)

modUI <- function(id) {
