I often find my self writing custom inputs with `tags` or `HTML` because I want to alter some attribute. A set of functions that modifies 'shiny.tag' objects would make it easier to use the existing shiny input and then just modify specific attributes. I made this function I find quite useful. 

```
alterAttrib <- function (
  attrib, pattern, replacement, ..., 
  recursiveOn =  c("div", "input", "select")) {

  res <- tagList(...)
  if (length(res) < 1) return(res)
  #print(class(res))

  for (i in 1:length(res)) {
    #print(paste(i, class(res[[i]])))
    if (!inherits((res[[i]]), "shiny.tag")) next

    if (!is.null(res[[i]]$attribs[[attrib]]))
      res[[i]]$attribs[[attrib]] <- gsub(pattern, replacement, res[[i]]$attribs[[attrib]])

    if (length(res[[i]]$children)>0) {
      for (j in 1:length(res[[i]]$children)) {
        if (!inherits(res[[i]]$children[[j]], "shiny.tag") ||
            !(res[[i]]$children[[j]]$name %in% recursiveOn))
          next
        res[[i]]$children[j] <- alterAttribs(attrib, pattern, replacement, (res[[i]]$children[[j]]))
      }
    }
  }
  res
}
```

It can be used like this:
```
alterAttrib("class", "form-group", "form-group form-group-sm", flowLayout(
  numericInput("num", "Number", 10),
  selectInput("unit", "Unit", c("m3/s"="m3s"), selectize=F)),
  recursiveOn = c("div")
)
```
Produces inputs with standard shiny inputs but alters the result to use smaller bootstrap class by changing all occurrences of "form-group" to "form-group form-group-sm" in attributes of "class", set to be recursive as long as the child has name=="div".

