Because JSON does not support `Infinity`, this will fail:

``` r
library(shiny)
runApp(list(
  ui = fluidPage(dataTableOutput('foo')),
  server = function(input, output) {
    output$foo = renderDataTable({
      as.data.frame(matrix(c(Inf, 1, NaN, 2, NaN, Inf), 2))
    })
  }
))
```

In the special case of DataTables, we may use the hack `toJSON(..., .inf = '"&infin;"')` for +Inf, but it won't work for -Inf. We can certainly use `.inf = 'null'` to hide infinity values, but that does not sound like a good idea, either. Note NaN is converted to null.

