When I create sets of tabPanels dynamically, they are sometimes linked to the wrong content.  In the example below, I scavenge CSV files and present them by directory.  The approach works if all CSV are nested to the same level.  But if one file is nested at a higher directory level, all tabPanels, though correctly named, display that file (in this case tail.csv).  The same is true if I strip dots from the input/output names.

``` R
library(shiny)
dir.create('files')
write.csv(head(Theoph),'files/head.csv',row.names=FALSE)
write.csv(tail(Theoph),'tail.csv',row.names=FALSE)
files <- dir(full.names=TRUE, recursive=TRUE, pattern='\\.csv$')
ui <- pageWithSidebar(
  headerPanel=headerPanel('data'), 
  sidebarPanel=sidebarPanel(
    radioButtons('dirname','directory',unique(dirname(files)))
  ),
  mainPanel(
    uiOutput("tabsets") # https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/shiny-discuss/-xSng1348MU
  )
)
server <- function(input,output,session){
   output$tabsets <- renderUI({
     f <- reactive({files[dirname(files) == input$dirname]})
     tabs <- lapply(f(), function(nm)tabPanel(title=basename(nm),dataTableOutput(nm)))
     do.call(tabsetPanel, c(tabs))
   })
   for(f in files)output[[f]] <- renderDataTable(read.csv(f))
}
runApp(list(ui=ui,server=server))
